#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:224
msgid "Show rulers"
msgstr "Dangos mesuryddion"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:225
msgid ""
"When checked, both vertical and horizontal rulers are shown on the "
"KPresenter slide (this is the default). When unchecked, the rulers are not "
"shown on any slide."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:229
msgid "Show status bar"
msgstr "Dangos y bar cyflwr"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:230
msgid "Toggle the statusbar, which is shown by default."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:237
msgid "Number of recent files:"
msgstr "Nifer y ffeiliau diweddar:"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:238
msgid ""
"Set the number of recent files which will be opened using the File->Open "
"Recent menu. Default is to remember 10 filenames. The maximum you can set is "
"20 and the minimum is 1."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:249
msgid "Text indentation depth:"
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:250
msgid ""
"This setting is used by Increase Depth and Decrease Depth menu items (in the "
"Text menu) to change the indentation depth. The Default is 1 centimeter."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:321
msgid "Background object color:"
msgstr "Lliw gwrthrych cefndir:"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:322
msgid ""
"Change the background color of the text box. The background is white by "
"default. If you have a dark background color and you want to put some white "
"text on it, you can change the color of the text box so that you can see "
"what you are typing. When you have finished, the area around the text will "
"revert to the background color. The Defaults button restores the original "
"settings."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:334
msgid "Grid color:"
msgstr "Lliw grid:"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:335
msgid "Here you can change the grid color, which is black by default."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:432
msgid "Undo/redo limit:"
msgstr "Datwneud/ailwneud y terfyn:"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:434
msgid ""
"Set the number of actions you can undo and redo (how many actions KPresenter "
"keeps in its Undo buffer). This ranges from a minimum of 10 to a maximum of "
"60 (the default is 30). Once the number of actions reaches the number set "
"here, earlier actions will be forgotten."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:439
msgid "Display links"
msgstr "Dangos cysylltau"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:440
msgid ""
"When you want to include a link in your slide, you can use the Insert-"
">Link... menu, which allows you to insert URL, mail or file links. If the "
"option Display links is checked, all links will be active and displayed in a "
"different color (this is the default behavior). If the option is unchecked, "
"the links will be inactive and the same color as the text. This affects both "
"the edited slides and the slide show."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:444
msgid "&Underline all links"
msgstr "&Tanlinellu pob cyswllt"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:446
msgid ""
"If this is checked, all links will be underlined (this is the default). If "
"it is not checked, the links will not be underlined."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:450
msgid "Display comments"
msgstr "Dangos sylwadau"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:452
msgid ""
"Comments are inserted in the text at the cursor using the Insert->Comment... "
"menu. Comments can only be viewed in edit mode and not in the slide show. If "
"this option is checked (default) then each comment will be shown as a small "
"yellow rectangle. You can then right-click on them to edit them, remove them "
"or copy the text."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:455
msgid "Display field code"
msgstr "Dangos côd maes"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:457
msgid ""
"In editor mode (not in slide show) this option will display all the variable "
"codes as well as Link at links location. This is very useful to see what "
"variable is displayed. Variables are inserted using the Insert -> Variable "
"menu."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:460
msgid "Print slide notes"
msgstr "Argraffu nodiadau tryloywder"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:462
msgid ""
"If checked, all notes will be printed on paper. The notes will all be "
"printed separately on the last page, from the first slide to the last and "
"finally the Master Page Note. You can see the notes for each slide using the "
"View->Show notebar menu."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:467
msgid "Grid"
msgstr "Grid"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:473
msgid "Horizontal grid size:"
msgstr "Maint llorweddol y grid:"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:474
msgid ""
"Set the space in millimeters between two horizontal points on the grid. "
"Default is 5 millimeters."
msgstr ""

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:482
msgid "Vertical grid size:"
msgstr "Maint fertigol y grid:"

#: old/KPrConfig.cpp:483
msgid ""
"Set the space in millimeters between two vertical points on the grid. "
"Default is 5 millimeters."
msgstr ""

